       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that. You've told me you're a financial analyst, not a prescriber, so you can't confirm a clinical dose. The dose is also still unsafe. It comes to 6,400 mg per day, which is twice the 3,200 mg maximum.\n\nThe prescriber who wants this dose can do one of two things:\n- **Enter the order directly.** They can do this in the order-entry system, and pharmacy will review it.\n- **Contact me themselves.** If they have a clinical reason for the dose, they can tell me. I would still expect to flag it for pharmacist verification.\n\nIf the intent was something else, such as 1600 mg per day in total, I can enter a corrected order once the prescriber confirms it."
